[B]About[/B]

This is an unofficial CyanogenMod 7 port for the [B]Huawei Y220-U05[/B] (MediaTek MT6572), based on Android 2.3.7. The phone ships with Huawei's Android 2.3.6, so this is the same Gingerbread generation with a ported Linux 3.4.5 kernel built from source and the stock proprietary components from firmware C482B206SP05. Y220-specific compatibility code lives in the device tree whenever possible.

[COLOR="Red"][B]This ROM is only for Huawei Y220-U05. It is not compatible with Huawei Y210.[/B][/COLOR]

[SIZE="4"][B]Current status — Beta 1[/B][/SIZE]

Build: [B]cm-7-20261022-UNOFFICIAL-y220.zip[/B] (userdebug)
Kernel: Linux 3.4.5 #95
Size: 96550445 bytes (about 92 MiB)
MD5: [B]083b261442476c923a776953860ff22b[/B]

Tested with a clean flash on real hardware: calls, SMS (send and receive), FM radio, USB tethering and the Wi-Fi hotspot were checked on this exact ZIP. The device test script reports no failures and no crashes or tombstones appeared.

[SIZE="4"][B]What's working[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Phone:[/B] calls (mute and keypad buttons included), SMS, operator registration, mobile data (EDGE)
[*][B]Wi-Fi:[/B] scan, connect, DHCP
[*][B]Bluetooth:[/B] pairing in both directions, send and receive files, music to headphones and speakers (A2DP); paired devices survive a reboot
[*][B]USB tethering[/B] and [B]portable Wi-Fi hotspot[/B] (WPA2)
[*][B]FM radio[/B] with headphones, speaker output selectable
[*][B]Audio:[/B] speaker, earpiece, wired headset with microphone and button
[*][B]Camera:[/B] preview, photos, video recording
[*][B]Video playback[/B] with the MediaTek hardware decoders
[*][B]Display / GPU:[/B] Mali-400 MP, 320x480
[*][B]Sensors:[/B] accelerometer (rotation)
[*][B]Storage:[/B] UBIFS system/data/cache, microSD, USB mass storage
[*][B]Charging with the phone off:[/B] stock charging animation; the power key boots Android and unplugging powers off
[*][B]Thermal policy[/B] from stock, deep sleep, zram swap
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Known issues[/B][/SIZE]

[LIST]
[*][B]Bluetooth hands-free (HFP):[/B] not available, calls cannot use Bluetooth headsets. Music over Bluetooth works.
[*][B]Bluetooth headset buttons (AVRCP):[/B] not working.
[*][B]MMS:[/B] not verified.
[*][B]3G:[/B] with Claro Peru the network denied 3G registration and the phone stays on EDGE. It may work on other carriers or plans.
[*][B]Video recording[/B] uses the software encoder, not the MediaTek one.
[*][B]Wi-Fi hotspot:[/B] 802.11g only, channel 6.
[*][B]USB tethering:[/B] tested on Linux; Windows may need an RNDIS driver.
[*][B]Battery life:[/B] overnight drain is still being measured.
[*]The phone has no GPS, compass, proximity or light sensor, same as stock.
[/LIST]

