[SIZE="4"][B]Installation[/B][/SIZE]

[COLOR="Red"][B]Back up NVRAM (IMEI, Wi-Fi and Bluetooth addresses) and your complete stock system before flashing. Do not use Format All in SP Flash Tool, and do not use SP Flash Tool v6.[/B][/COLOR]

[LIST=1]
[*]Install [URL="https://xdaforums.com/t/recovery-unofficial-twrp-3-1-1-0-1-for-huawei-y220-u05.4805984/"]TWRP 3.1.1-0.1 for Huawei Y220-U05[/URL].
[*]Copy the ROM ZIP to the external microSD.
[*]Boot into TWRP and make a complete backup to the external microSD.
[*]Wipe data/factory reset, cache and Dalvik cache.
[*]Install cm-7-20261022-UNOFFICIAL-y220.zip.
[*]Reboot. The first boot takes a few minutes.
[*]Optional: flash Gingerbread (2.3) gapps.
[/LIST]

[B]Updating from an earlier CM7 build:[/B] make a backup, wipe cache and Dalvik cache, install the new ZIP and reboot. A clean flash is recommended when coming from the 2026-10-13 build.

[B]UBIFS warning:[/B] install the ZIP from TWRP. Do not write the loose system.img directly to MTD14. The installer safely empties the existing system UBIFS volume, copies the ROM, and writes the MTK-formatted boot image. It does not replace TWRP.

[B]Charging with the phone off:[/B] power off, unplug, wait until the screen is black, then plug in the charger. If you power off with the charger already connected, the bootloader restarts into Android.

[COLOR="Red"][SIZE="5"][CENTER]Do not mirror the download without permission.[/CENTER][/SIZE][/COLOR]

