[SIZE="4"][B]Bug reports[/B][/SIZE]

Please include:

[LIST]
[*]Exact phone model and original firmware version
[*]Clean flash or update from an older build
[*]Recovery version used
[*]Steps required to reproduce the problem
[*]Relevant logcat and, for kernel issues, dmesg (or /proc/last_kmsg after a hang)
[*]Whether the problem also happens after a clean flash
[/LIST]

[SIZE="4"][B]Changelog[/B][/SIZE]

[B]2026-10-22 — Beta 1[/B]

[LIST]
[*]Bluetooth: send and receive files, music to headphones (A2DP), device class and paired devices kept across reboots, unpair
[*]USB tethering and portable Wi-Fi hotspot (kernel netfilter, hostapd 0.8 over nl80211)
[*]Charging with the phone off: fixed a kernel hang; the power key now boots Android
[*]Hardware video decoding with the MediaTek decoders
[*]In-call mute and keypad buttons, call audio, headset button
[*]Stock thermal policy, 24 MB Dalvik heap
[*]FM radio app signed correctly in userdebug builds
[*]Touch firmware update interface removed (any app could reflash the touch controller)
[*]userdebug build
[/LIST]

[B]2026-10-13 — first public beta candidate[/B]

[LIST]
[*]Complete TWRP-installable build tested on real Y220-U05 hardware
[*]Ported Linux 3.4.5 kernel with working modem, NAND partition layout, zram and reduced debug logging
[*]UBIFS-aware boot and installation path
[*]MediaTek RIL integration with calls, SMS and EDGE data
[*]Y220 audio HAL for speaker output and microphone input
[*]MediaTek Wi-Fi loader and private WEXT compatibility moved into the device tree
[*]MediaTek Bluetooth power, discovery and pairing bridge
[*]Stock camera stack integrated through device-owned compatibility layers
[*]Fixed YV12 camera preview and MediaTek I420 video recording
[/LIST]

